3fu51Sx2lzcOJ6A" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">pumped by Bournemouth</a> to sen=
d the latest patsy handed the reins towards the door marked =E2=80=9CDo One=
=E2=80=9D, Carrick was applauded by the Stretford End, and Old Trafford=E2=
=80=99s stands east, south and north. A proud man walking, as Claudio Ranie=
ri once described the fate of the manager who knows the end is approaching.=
 Among the paying public, on the long list of those held responsible for th=
e latest betrayal of a legend, Carrick is towards the bottom. If even on it=
. Those heading the list felt their ears burn in a atmosphere crackling wit=
h mutiny.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Once Carrick=E2=80=99s head dipped below t=
he tunnel, the players behind him on the walk of shame learned their place =
in the hierarchy of culpability. Boos and insults rained down on the latest=
 unfortunates to wear the red shirt. Bruno Fernandes, talisman turned turnc=
oat, arrived at Old Trafford knowing his outburst in Como had led to his de=
-selection. The former fan favourite, last season=E2=80=99s player of the y=
ear, hardly heard his name sung all afternoon. Et tu, Bruno? <a href=3D"htt=
ps://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ=
7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPg4Po31vrjVzXiEA_Xskplj8mHDkyl38Ni17jx0s=
w9gjw34PyF1SgLQpABl-jJa8_vyHQJftwFOzUi6lF680QqpNPEtCRX25v_yxKazbFR0ZHM6G9aa=
